    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "estop", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "M2M_PEER", "kind": "move", "scope": "estop", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "role" |
    | {"now": 1000} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "GUEST", "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "refuse" | "role" |
    | {"now": 1000} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "RESUME"} | "execute" | "resume" |
    | {"now": 1000, "estopped": true} | {"id": "c1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "M2M_PEER", "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP_CLEAR"} | "refuse" | "role" |
    | {"now": 1000, "estopped": true} | {"id": "c1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "M2M_TRUSTED", "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP_CLEAR"} | "execute" | "estop_clear" |

req GT-007 "Level of assurance"
  decision D-009, D-010
  text
    The level of assurance (LoA) of a command is its `loa` when it has one; otherwise it is `2`
    when its `tier` is `"authoritative"`, and `1` in every other case (RCAN §8.7). The level a
    command needs is the state's `minLoaControl`; when its scope, lowercased as in REQ-GT-006,
    is `safety`, it is the greater of `minLoaControl` and `minLoaSafety`. A command whose level
    is below the level it needs MUST be refused as `loa`. A status query needs no level, and an
    ESTOP never comes to this step (REQ-GT-003).
  table decide
    | state | command | result.decision | result.reason |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "loa": 2, "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "tier": "authoritative", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 3, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "tier": "authoritative", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "tier": "community", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "tier": "root", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "loa": 1, "tier": "authoritative", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "GUEST", "kind": "move", "scope": "chat", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 3} | {"id": "q1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "GUEST", "kind": "status"} | "execute" | "status" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 2} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "loa": 3, "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "execute" | "stop" |
    | {"now": 1000, "estopped": true, "minLoaSafety": 3} | {"id": "c1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "loa": 2, "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP_CLEAR"} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "estopped": true, "minLoaSafety": 3} | {"id": "c1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "loa": 3, "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP_CLEAR"} | "execute" | "estop_clear" |
    | {"now": 1000, "estopped": true, "minLoaControl": 2, "minLoaSafety": 1} | {"id": "c1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "loa": 1, "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP_CLEAR"} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaSafety": 3, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "loa": 2, "kind": "move", "scope": "SAFETY", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "loa" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaSafety": 3, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "CREATOR", "loa": 2, "kind": "move", "scope": "estop", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "minLoaControl": 3} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "GUEST", "loa": 1, "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "refuse" | "role" |

req GT-008 "STOP and RESUME"
  decision D-005
  text
    A STOP that passes the earlier steps MUST be carried out (`execute`, `stop`) and sets
    `stopped` to `true`; a RESUME that passes them MUST be carried out (`execute`, `resume`) and
    sets `stopped` to `false`. Neither changes `estopped`, and neither depends on what `stopped`
    was. While `stopped` is `true`, a move MUST be refused as `stopped`.
  table decide
    | state | command | result.decision | result.reason | result.state.stopped |
    | {"now": 1000} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "execute" | "stop" | true |
    | {"now": 1000, "stopped": true} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "STOP"} | "execute" | "stop" | true |
    | {"now": 1000, "stopped": true} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "RESUME"} | "execute" | "resume" | false |
    | {"now": 1000} | {"id": "s1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "safety", "event": "RESUME"} | "execute" | "resume" | false |
    | {"now": 1000, "stopped": true, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "stopped" | true |
    | {"now": 1000, "stopped": true} | {"id": "q1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "GUEST", "kind": "status"} | "execute" | "status" | true |

req GT-009 "Joint limits"
  decision D-006
  text
    A move's targets MUST be checked one at a time, in their order, each with these checks in
    this order; the first check that fails refuses the move:

    1. a joint that is not a member of the state's `limits` (as a name: with no member
       `toString` in `limits`, a joint `toString` is not in it): `unknown_joint`;
    2. a joint that an earlier target of the same move named: `duplicate_joint`;
    3. a position below the joint's `min` or above its `max`: `limits`. A position equal to
       `min` or to `max` is within the limits.
  table decide
    | state | command | result.decision | result.reason |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 1}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": -1}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 1.0000001}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "limits" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "elbow", "position": -0.5}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "limits" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "gripper", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "Base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}, {"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "duplicate_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 5}, {"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "limits" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "elbow", "position": 1}, {"joint": "base", "position": 0}, {"joint": "elbow", "position": 9}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "duplicate_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}, {"joint": "gripper", "position": 0}, {"joint": "base", "position": 9}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}, "elbow": {"min": 0, "max": 2}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "elbow", "position": 2}, {"joint": "base", "position": -1}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "toString", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "__proto__", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "hasOwnProperty", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "unknown_joint" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"__proto__": {"min": 0, "max": 1}, "toString": {"min": 0, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "__proto__", "position": 1}, {"joint": "toString", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"__proto__": {"min": 0, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "__proto__", "position": 2}], "speed": 0} | "refuse" | "limits" |

req GT-010 "Speed"
  decision D-008
  text
    A move whose `speed` is greater than the state's `maxSpeed` MUST be refused as `speed`. A
    speed equal to `maxSpeed` is allowed. With no `maxSpeed` in the state it is 0
    (REQ-RQ-002), so only a move at speed 0 gets past this step.
  table decide
    | state | command | result.decision | result.reason |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 1} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 1.5} | "refuse" | "speed" |
    | {"now": 1000, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0.001} | "refuse" | "speed" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 0, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |

req GT-011 "Confidence gates"
  decision D-007, D-011, D-012
  text
    The gate of a move is the member of the state's `gates` whose name is the move's scope,
    lowercased as in REQ-GT-006; when `gates` has no member of that name, the move has no
    gate. A move that has a gate and a `confidence` below the gate's `min` MUST be refused as
    `confidence` when the gate's `onFail` is `"block"`, and held (`hold`, `confidence`) when it
    is `"escalate"`. A confidence equal to `min` passes. A move without `confidence` passes
    every gate.
  table decide
    | state | command | result.decision | result.reason |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "refuse" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.75} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.7499999} | "refuse" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "escalate"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "hold" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "Control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "refuse" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"Control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "Control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "teleop", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"kick": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "Kick", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "refuse" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"kick": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "Kick", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "toString", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0, "onFail": "block"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0} | "execute" | "ok" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 1, "onFail": "escalate"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.9} | "hold" | "confidence" |
    | {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 1, "onFail": "escalate"}}} | {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 1} | "execute" | "ok" |
  example decide {"state": {"now": 1000, "maxSpeed": 1, "limits": {"base": {"min": -1, "max": 1}}, "gates": {"control": {"min": 0.75, "onFail": "escalate"}}}, "command": {"id": "m1", "timestamp": 1000, "role": "OPERATOR", "kind": "move", "scope": "control", "targets": [{"joint": "base", "position": 0}], "speed": 0, "confidence": 0.5}}
    expect result.state.seen = [{"id": "m1", "expires": 1030}]
    expect result.state.estopped = false
    expect result.state.stopped = false

note
  text
    The properties below are checked on generated states and commands: the types whose names
    start with `sample` say what is drawn. They are a choice of test inputs (the clock at 1000,
    a few joints, scopes and IDs that collide), not a limit on what a request may hold, which
    REQ-RQ-002 and REQ-RQ-003 give.

property GT-P1 "An ESTOP is always carried out"
  supports GT-003
  samples 200
  for s in sampleState
  for c in sampleSafety
  call a = decide {"state": s, "command": {"id": c.id, "timestamp": c.timestamp, "role": c.role, "kind": "safety", "event": "ESTOP"}}
  expect a.result.decision == "execute" and a.result.reason == "estop" and a.result.state.estopped == true

property GT-P2 "While e-stopped, nothing that could move the robot is carried out"
  supports GT-005
  samples 200
  for s in sampleState
  for c in sampleCommand
  where has(s, "estopped") and s.estopped
  call a = decide {"state": s, "command": c}
  expect has(a, "error") or a.result.decision != "execute" or c.kind == "status" or (c.kind == "safety" and c.event != "RESUME")

property GT-P3 "Only an executed safety event changes a latch"
  supports GT-001, GT-005, GT-008
  samples 300
  for s in sampleState
  for c in sampleCommand
  call a = decide {"state": s, "command": c}
  expect has(a, "error") or (a.result.decision == "execute" and c.kind == "safety") or (a.result.state.estopped == (has(s, "estopped") and s.estopped) and a.result.state.stopped == (has(s, "stopped") and s.stopped))

property GT-P4 "A message ID works once"
  supports GT-004
  samples 300
  for s in sampleState
  for c in sampleCommand
  call a = decide {"state": s, "command": c}
  call b = decide {"state": has(a, "result") ? a.result.state : s, "command": c}
  expect has(a, "error") or a.result.reason == "estop" or a.result.reason == "stale" or a.result.reason == "future" or b.result.reason == "replay"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
section BU "The implementation folder"
  text
    These requirements are checked on the implementation folder, not through the driver.

req BU-001 "REGEN.json"
  text
    The implementation folder MUST contain `REGEN.json`, a JSON object with exactly the keys
    `lang` (`"ts"` or `"py"`), `build`, `test` and `driver`. Each of `build`, `test` and
    `driver` is a command string, or an object whose keys are Node.js `process.platform` values
    (such as `"win32"`) plus a required `"default"`, each mapping to a command string. Commands
    run in the implementation folder. `build` and `test` run through the platform shell; an
    empty `build` means there is nothing to build. `driver` is split on single spaces and
    started without a shell, so it MUST be plain space-separated words. The same REGEN.json
    MUST work on Windows and on Linux.
  static json "REGEN.json" matches {lang: "ts" | "py", build: string | {default: string, ...}, test: string | {default: string, ...}, driver: string | {default: string, ...}}

req BU-002 "Own tests"
  text
    The implementation MUST have its own tests, including at least one for every MUST in this
    document, and the command `REGEN.json` names as `test` MUST pass.
  static command test exits 0 within 300

req BU-003 "Runtime and dependencies"
  text
    TypeScript MUST run on Node.js 22.18 or later directly by type stripping: erasable syntax
    only, no build step, relative imports with the `.ts` extension. Python MUST run on 3.11 or
    later. Only the language's standard library is used: nothing is installed, and a
    `package.json`, if there is one, declares no dependencies.
  static file "node_modules", "package-lock.json", "requirements.txt", "Pipfile", "poetry.lock" absent
  static text "package.json" not matching "\"(dev|peer|optional)?[dD]ependencies\""

req BU-004 "Size"
  text
    At most 500 non-blank lines of source in all: `.ts .mts .mjs .js` or `.py` files under the
    implementation folder, not counting tests (`*.test.*`, `*_test.*`, `test_*.py`, and anything
    under a `test/` or `tests/` folder).
  static lines "**/*.ts", "**/*.mts", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.js", "**/*.py" at most 500 excluding "**/*.test.*", "**/*_test.*", "**/test_*.py", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
open OP-001 "Numbers outside binary64"
  text
    A JSON number in a request too large for a binary64 value (such as `1e400`), anywhere in
    the request: whether it is a `bad_request`, and what the next state holds for it.

open OP-002 "Standard error and error text"
  text
    What the driver writes to standard error; any human-readable error text, which never
    appears in a response.

open OP-003 "Odd request bytes"
  text
    Request bytes that are not valid UTF-8, and duplicate member names in a JSON object.

open OP-004 "The size of the replay set"
  text
    How many entries `seen` may hold. rcan-ts drops the oldest entry when its replay cache
    holds 10,000; this gate keeps every unexpired entry it is given, and the caller decides how
    large a state it keeps.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
decision D-001 "A pure function of state and command"
  source CONFIDENCE.md, claim 5; rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/replay.ts
  text
    rcan-ts keeps its replay cache inside an object and reads the clock with `Date.now()`. A
    gate written that way cannot be judged request by request: its answer depends on what came
    before and on when it runs. Decision: the state goes in with every command and comes back
    out, and the clock is a member of the state (`now`). Why: every answer is then a function
    of its request, so a suite can check it and two implementations can be compared on the
    same requests.
  rejected "A gate that keeps its state between requests: the suite would have to replay whole sessions, and one wrong answer would change every later one."

decision D-002 "An ESTOP is never blocked, by anything"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/safety.ts ("Protocol 66 safety invariant: ESTOP is NEVER blocked by new mechanisms"); rcan.dev/docs/safety ("ESTOP is always accepted regardless of clock sync state", "ESTOP is always exempt from LoA enforcement")
  text
    RCAN states the rule for each mechanism in turn: clock synchronization, level of
    assurance, and new mechanisms in general. Decision: the ESTOP comes before every check,
    freshness and replay included, and is carried out even when the latch is already set. It
    does not use up its ID, since nothing is ever refused as a replayed ESTOP. Why: a stale or
    repeated ESTOP that stops a robot costs little; a real one that is refused can cost a
    great deal.
  rejected "Apply the replay check to ESTOP like any other message: a retransmitted ESTOP, sent because the first seemed lost, would be refused."

decision D-003 "Freshness and replay come first, and an ID is used up whatever follows"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/replay.ts (ReplayCache.checkAndRecord records an ID as soon as it passes the freshness check)
  text
    In rcan-ts the replay cache is separate from authorization: an ID that passes it is
    recorded, whatever happens to the message later. Decision: freshness and replay are steps
    2 and 3, before the latches, roles, assurance and limits, and the ID is used up at step 3.
    Why: a message ID names one message; a refused message sent again is still the same
    message, and refusing it as a replay tells its sender to send a new one.
  rejected "Use up an ID only when the command is carried out: a sender could then repeat a refused command until the robot's state changed under it."

decision D-004 "A 10-second cap for safety messages and 5 seconds of drift"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/replay.ts (DEFAULT_WINDOW_S 30, SAFETY_MAX_WINDOW_S 10, "Allow 5s future drift for clock skew"); rcan.dev/docs/safety, §8.4 ("Maximum drift tolerance: ±5 seconds")
  text
    Decision: the window defaults to 30 seconds; safety messages use at most 10; a timestamp
    up to 5 seconds ahead of the clock is fresh. A command is stale only when strictly older
    than the window, an entry expires when `expires` is not after `now`, and the new entry
    expires at `now + w`, as rcan-ts does. Why: these are the SDK's numbers and comparisons.
  rejected "Expire the new entry at timestamp + w: shorter, but not what rcan-ts does."

decision D-005 "STOP and RESUME are control commands; ESTOP_CLEAR needs the safety scope"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/safety.ts ("ESTOP requires explicit hardware-level clear; RESUME only clears STOP"); rcan.dev/docs/safety ("the robot remains stopped until an operator explicitly clears it via an authenticated ESTOP_CLEAR command"); rcan.dev/docs/identity, LoA matrix ("safety (ESTOP_CLEAR, config safety overrides)")
  text
    rcan-ts leaves clearing an ESTOP to hardware; the RCAN documents describe an
    authenticated ESTOP_CLEAR command in the `safety` scope. Neither says which scope a STOP or
    a RESUME needs. Decision: the gate has ESTOP_CLEAR, in the `safety` scope (CREATOR, and the
    safety level of assurance); STOP and RESUME are in the `control` scope (OPERATOR). While
    e-stopped, a STOP goes through (it can only make the robot safer, and it holds the robot
    after the clear), a RESUME does not. Why: an operator who can drive the robot can stop it;
    only the role that may change safety settings can undo an emergency stop.
  rejected "No ESTOP_CLEAR in the gate, as in rcan-ts: then the caller must change estopped by hand, and nothing in the gate checks who did."
  rejected "STOP in the safety scope: an operator could drive the robot and not stop it."

decision D-006 "Names are looked up as names"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/identity.ts (validateRoleForScope), run on 2026-10-08
  text
    rcan-ts looks scopes up in a plain JavaScript object, so a scope named `constructor` or
    `__proto__` finds a member that every object inherits, and is refused for every role,
    M2M_TRUSTED included, where its own rule says an unknown scope needs OPERATOR. The same
    kind of lookup on joint names would let a joint named `toString` through with no limits at
    all. Decision: scopes, joints and gates are looked up only among the names the tables and
    the state hold, and examples pin the inherited names. Why: the stated rule is the
    intended one, and a lookup that finds inherited members fails differently in each
    language.
  rejected "Follow rcan-ts and refuse constructor and __proto__ for every role: it fails safe, but it is a lookup accident, and Python implementations would not reproduce it."

decision D-007 "Scopes are lowercased in ASCII only"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/identity.ts (SCOPE_MIN_ROLE[scope.toLowerCase()])
  text
    rcan-ts lowercases a scope with JavaScript's `toLowerCase`, which also maps letters
    outside ASCII: the KELVIN SIGN, U+212A, becomes the ASCII `k`. Languages and Unicode
    versions differ in such mappings. Decision: only `A` to `Z` are lowercased. Why: every
    scope name RCAN defines is ASCII, and the answer then does not depend on the language or
    its Unicode tables.
  rejected "Unicode lowercasing: the same scope could get different gates in different implementations."

decision D-008 "What the gate is not told, it does not allow"
  source rcan.dev/docs/identity, §8.7 (min_loa_for_control defaults to 1); rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/replay.ts (window 30)
  text
    RCAN gives defaults for the level of assurance (1) and the replay window (30 seconds), and
    the gate uses them. It gives none for joint limits or a speed limit. Decision: with no
    `limits`, no joint is known and every move is refused; with no `maxSpeed`, the limit is
    0. Confidence gates default to none, since each gate only adds a refusal. Why: a gate
    that forgets its configuration should stop the robot, not free it.
  rejected "Unlimited speed without maxSpeed: a missing member would remove a safety limit."

decision D-009 "The LoA minimum applies to every command that acts"
  source rcan.dev/docs/identity, §8.7 (prose: "a minimum identity assurance level for control-scope commands"; pseudocode check_loa: required_loa = min_loa_for_control for every message; enforcement matrix: status, discover and observer at LoA 1)
  text
    The RCAN document says min_loa_for_control is for control-scope commands, but its
    pseudocode applies it to every message, and its matrix recommends LoA 1 for status
    queries. Decision: every command except a status query (and an ESTOP) needs
    `minLoaControl`, raised to `minLoaSafety` in the `safety` scope. Why: a move in another
    scope (`teleop`, or one this gate does not know) moves the robot as much as a `control`
    one; a status query moves nothing.
  rejected "Only the scope control: a teleop move from an unverified sender would pass."
  rejected "Every message, status queries too: contradicts the matrix's LoA 1 for status."

decision D-010 "A root-tier sender without loa has level 1"
  source rcan.dev/docs/identity, §8.7 (defaults when loa is absent: authoritative 2, community 1, neither field present 1)
  text
    The document gives no default for a token from a root registry that carries no `loa`.
    Decision: 1, as for every case the document does not raise to 2. Why: when the level is
    unknown, the lowest is the safe assumption; a root registry that vouches for more can say
    so in `loa`.
  rejected "3, a root registry being the most trusted tier: trusts what the token does not say."

decision D-011 "A confidence equal to the minimum passes"
  source rcan-ts at b563fb5, src/gates.ts (allows: confidence >= threshold); rcan-py at b718bf3, rcan/gates.py (confidence >= self.threshold); rcan.dev/docs/safety ("Block command if AI confidence < 0.75"); against: rcan.dev/spec/v1.2 changelog ("ConfidenceGate now rejects exactly-at-threshold values (strict <)")
  text
    Both SDKs and the safety document allow a confidence equal to the threshold; one line of
    the v1.2 changelog says the opposite. Decision: equal passes. Why: three sources, two of
    them running code, against one changelog line, which may mean that the strict comparison
    is the one that rejects.
  rejected "Reject at the threshold, as the changelog line reads: both SDKs would disagree with the gate on every boundary value."

decision D-012 "A command without confidence passes the gates"
  source rcan.dev/docs/safety (brain.confidence_gates: "Per-scope AI confidence thresholds"; on_fail block or escalate); rcan.dev/conformance (L2-CONF-001 and L2-CONF-002)
  text
    RCAN's confidence gates are thresholds on the confidence of the AI brain, blocking or
    escalating to a person a command the model was unsure of. A command a person gave carries
    no model confidence. Decision: gates apply only to moves that carry `confidence`;
    `escalate` holds the move (`hold`), and `block` refuses it. Why: the gate is about the
    model's certainty; a person's command is checked by role and assurance instead.
  rejected "Treat a missing confidence as 0: every command a person gave in a gated scope would be held or refused."
